  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Capacitaci&#xf3;n y colocaci&#xf3;n laboral para posibles migrantes</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Skills for employment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(El Salvador):  The Skills for Employment activity will equip likely migrants, returnees, and vulnerable populations with social-emotional and technical skills for employment. It will prepare youth for new and better employment opportunities by matching workforce skill needs with technical and vocational training in collaboration with the private sector, government agencies, and civil society. The activity will provide youth with stipends, mentorship, and technical and life skills. It will work with local service providers and actors to contribute to the Central American Service Corps initiative. In addition, the activity aims to support vulnerable groups, including youth, LGBTQI+ individuals, people with disabilities, and returned migrants, in prioritized locales through training, work experience, and job placement support, reducing vulnerabilities and promoting inclusion.The activity will increase private sector participation to improve the enabling environment for employment. The relevance and quality of technical education will be increased to support youth in job placement. Out-of-school individuals will be given the opportunity to complete their formal education. Education service providers will increase their institutional capacity to provide wraparound services such as psychosocial and trauma support, labor orientation, job search and placement assistance, coaching in the hiring process, and links to entrepreneurship resources. The activity will build the capacity of local sub-recipients, conducting all activity implementation through them so that they are more capable and likely to eventually receive a direct award from USAID. The activity addresses ICS MO 3.2 and RCS Pillar I by strengthening El Salvador&apos;s capacity to promote inclusive human capital development. By strengthening the capacity of local organizations, it also supports Agency localization priorities.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El objetivo de esta APS es asociarse con numerosas partes interesadas para contribuir al logro de la meta 2020-2025 de la Estrategia de Cooperaci&#xf3;n para el Desarrollo Nacional (CDCS) de USAID/El Salvador. Este objetivo es reducir los factores que impulsan la migraci&#xf3;n irregular fomentando un El Salvador m&#xe1;s autosuficiente: un El Salvador seguro, pr&#xf3;spero y bien gobernado.</narrative>
  </description>
